WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.557 --> 00:00:03.140
(upbeat music)

00:00:04.470 --> 00:00:05.370
- [Narrator] Cork.

00:00:06.360 --> 00:00:08.530
It's the miracle tree bark that's found

00:00:08.530 --> 00:00:12.130
in everything from baseball
bats to spaceships.

00:00:12.130 --> 00:00:14.660
But it's best known as the last obstacle

00:00:14.660 --> 00:00:16.233
in your journey to drink wine.

00:00:18.130 --> 00:00:21.910
Yes, sometimes de-corking
can feel like a chore.

00:00:21.910 --> 00:00:25.810
No, I'm not talking about
popping open a wine bottle.

00:00:25.810 --> 00:00:27.660
I'm talking about how cork is harvested

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:30.830
in the first place by these guys.

00:00:30.830 --> 00:00:33.900
Manual cork harvesters in Portugal.

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:37.860
It's a job so difficult and yet so artful,

00:00:37.860 --> 00:00:39.860
machines have yet to render it obsolete.

00:00:41.940 --> 00:00:42.700
(upbeat music)

00:00:48.240 --> 00:00:51.820
Welcome to Portugal where
cork is the national tree.

00:00:52.840 --> 00:00:55.430
Cork is native to the Mediterranean basin,

00:00:55.430 --> 00:00:58.043
but nowhere does it grow more than here.

00:01:09.127 --> 00:01:11.460
- [Narrator] Since cork
trees can live for 200 years,

00:01:11.460 --> 00:01:14.559
Goncalo's trees are the
exact same trees his parents,

00:01:14.559 --> 00:01:18.719
grandparents, and great
grandparents also cared for.

00:01:18.719 --> 00:01:21.302
(upbeat music)

00:02:26.988 --> 00:02:29.405
(calm music)

00:03:23.913 --> 00:03:25.950
- [Narrator] Once a tree is harvested,

00:03:25.950 --> 00:03:28.803
it won't be cut again
for another nine years.

00:03:30.260 --> 00:03:32.090
This keeps the bark healthy

00:03:32.090 --> 00:03:36.448
and the harvest tradition alive
for the generations to come.

00:03:36.448 --> 00:03:38.865
(calm music)

